   "id": "switching-test",
   "title": "Test circuit for measuring switching times",
   "page": 10,
   "fixture": true,
   "description": "Fixture for the propagation, enable and disable times. A pulse generator drives the input under test, terminated to ground by RT, which matches the generator's own output impedance. The output carries CL to ground (jig and probe capacitance counted in) and RL to the common of switch S1, which connects RL to VCC, to GND or to nothing according to the measurement in the test data table. For propagation delay the generator drives an nAn input; for enable and disable times it drives nOE.",
