 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Organisation",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Eight non-inverting buffers in two groups of four. 1OE gates outputs 1Y0 to 1Y3 and 2OE gates 2Y0 to 2Y3; the part works as a pair of 4-bit drivers or a single 8-bit driver."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output enable",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "With nOE LOW each output nYn follows its input nAn. With nOE HIGH the four outputs of that group are high-impedance whatever the inputs."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input thresholds",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 74AHC244 switches at CMOS levels that scale with VCC (VIH 3.85 V min and VIL 1.65 V max at 5.5 V). The 74AHCT244 switches at TTL levels, VIH 2.0 V min and VIL 0.8 V max across VCC 4.5 V to 5.5 V. An AHCT input held at VCC - 2.1 V draws up to 1.35 mA extra supply current at 25 °C (ΔICC)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Schmitt-trigger inputs",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "All inputs, data and enable, have Schmitt-trigger action. The recommended input rise and fall rate is at most 20 ns/V at VCC = 5.0 V ± 0.5 V, and at most 100 ns/V for the 74AHC244 at 3.3 V ± 0.3 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Overvoltage-tolerant inputs",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Inputs are overvoltage tolerant to 5.5 V, so the part can translate between systems on different supplies. Input leakage is specified with VI = 5.5 V for VCC from 0 V to 5.5 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output drive",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Outputs are specified at ±4.0 mA at VCC = 3.0 V and ±8.0 mA at VCC = 4.5 V; the absolute limit is ±25 mA per output, with 75 mA total through VCC and GND."
  },
  {
   "topic": "DHVQFN20 centre pad",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The DHVQFN20 exposed pad is not a ground pin and has no electrical or mechanical need for solder; a soldered land floats or connects to GND."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature range",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Characteristics are specified over -40 °C to +85 °C and over -40 °C to +125 °C, with typical figures at 25 °C."
  }
 ],
